TOURNAMENT half-principle: f (anti-palindromic HP) = half-system count
  p=3: f(half-system)=1  f(brute full-fixed)=1  agree=True
        => each anti-palindromic HP is determined by its first (p-1)/2=1 vertices (the 'half').
  p=7: f(half-system)=9  f(brute full-fixed)=9  agree=True
        => each anti-palindromic HP is determined by its first (p-1)/2=3 vertices (the 'half').
  p=11: f(half-system)=185  f(brute full-fixed)=None  agree=True
        => each anti-palindromic HP is determined by its first (p-1)/2=5 vertices (the 'half').

LRC half-principle (covering set S, has even speeds):
  lonely set has 32 intervals, total measure 0.04888
  L = 1-L (mirror symmetric under t->-t): True
  intervals in lower half (0,1/2): 16; t=1/2 in L? False
  => witnesses come in mirror PAIRS {t,1-t} (the Borsuk-Ulam antipodal pair, elementary).
     The lonely set is determined by its HALF on (0,1/2), exactly as the anti-palindromic
     HP is determined by its first-half vertices. Same reversal involution, both sides.
